<title>BELGIUM: Rise in EU industry output below U.S. level.</title>
<headline>Rise in EU industry output below U.S. level.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union industrial production rose 0.5 percent in the first quarter of 1997 compared with the previous three months, Eurostat, the EU statistics office, said on Thursday.</p>
<p>This is well below the increase in industrial output in both the United States, where it rose 1.5 percent, and Japan, up by 1.9 percent.</p>
<p>There were wide variations between the member states of the 15-nation EU, ranging from an increase of 2.3 percent in Sweden to a fall of 0.2 percent in Britain, the only country which registered a decline.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
